Write  a Windows powershell script code to scramble data for a txt file?
Creating a data scrambling script
Here's a simple PowerShell script that scrambles the characters in a text file while keeping the overall line structure intact.

param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
    [string]$InputPath,

    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
    [string]$OutputPath
)

if (-not (Test-Path -Path $InputPath -PathType Leaf)) {
    throw "Input file '$InputPath' does not exist."
}

Get-Content -Path $InputPath | ForEach-Object {
    $chars = $_.ToCharArray()
    $random = [System.Random]::new()
    for ($i = $chars.Length - 1; $i -gt 0; $i--) {
        $swap = $random.Next(0, $i + 1)
        $temp = $chars[$i]
        $chars[$i] = $chars[$swap]
        $chars[$swap] = $temp
    }
    -join $chars
} | Set-Content -Path $OutputPath

Write-Host "Scrambled text written to $OutputPath"
Save the script (for example as Scramble-Text.ps1), then run it:

powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\Scramble-Text.ps1 -InputPath original.txt -OutputPath scrambled.txt
